<article class="env-lemma" id="09WV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09WV">Lemma <span data-tag="09WV">4.33.12</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B} \to \mathcal{C}$ be functors between categories. If $\mathcal{A}$ is fibred over $\mathcal{B}$ and $\mathcal{B}$ is fibred over $\mathcal{C}$, then $\mathcal{A}$ is fibred over $\mathcal{C}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from the definitions and Lemma <a href="/tag/09WU" data-tag="09WU">4.33.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>